{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the manual marginalized mixture likelihood implemented with `target += log_sum_exp(...)` by the algebraically equivalent built-in Bernoulli likelihood `y ~ bernoulli(dot_product(cluster_weight, cluster_prob))`. This is exact because, for binary `y` and simplex weights `w`, `sum_k w[k] * Bernoulli(y | p[k]) = Bernoulli(y | sum_k w[k] * p[k])`. No data fields were added or changed.
","model_safe_stan":"// ForestDB translation: Dirichlet Process
// SafeStan-compatible rewrite: Bernoulli mixture collapsed to its exact Bernoulli marginal.
data {
  int<lower=1> K;
  int<lower=1> N;
  array[N] int<lower=0, upper=1> y;
}
parameters {
  simplex[K] cluster_weight;
  vector<lower=0, upper=1>[K] cluster_prob;
}
model {
  real mix_prob;

  cluster_weight ~ dirichlet(rep_vector(1.0 / K, K));
  cluster_prob ~ beta(1, 1);

  mix_prob = dot_product(cluster_weight, cluster_prob);
  y ~ bernoulli(mix_prob);
}
generated quantities {
  int<lower=1, upper=K> cluster = categorical_rng(cluster_weight);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"K":5,"N":5,"y":[0,1,1,1,1]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
